  bodyName: Mars
  classification: Terrestrial Planet
  positionFromSun: 4th Planet
  overview: Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun. It is a cold rocky world with
    a thin carbon dioxide atmosphere. Its surface contains enormous volcanoes deep
    canyons impact craters and geological evidence of ancient environments where
    liquid water may have existed.
  keyCharacteristics: 'Known as the Red Planet.

    Home to Olympus Mons a giant
    shield volcano.

    Contains Valles Marineris an enormous canyon system.

    Has
    polar ice caps.

    Two natural satellites: Phobos and Deimos.

    Evidence
    of ancient water activity.'
